== The Final Forty — Questions

#mcq(1, [Chromosomes are best seen during], [metaphase of mitosis], [interphase], [telophase], [G1 phase])

#mcq(2, [A woman with genotype X^H^X^h^ has a son. The probability that he is haemophilic is], [0], [1/2], [1/4], [1])

#mcq(3, [A gene mutation differs from a chromosome mutation in that a gene mutation], [changes the number of chromosomes], [moves part of a chromosome], [always affects the phenotype], [involves the sequence of bases in one gene])

#mcq(4, [Natural selection is best described as], [a random process with no direction], [a single event], [the differential survival and reproduction of variants], [a change in one gene])

#mcq(5, [Which would increase the accuracy of a quadrat estimate?], [Throwing the quadrat where the plants are thickest], [Increasing the number of random throws], [Using a bigger quadrat once], [Counting only one species])

#mcq(6, [Energy stored in the bodies of dead organisms is released mainly by], [photosynthesis], [evaporation], [respiration of decomposers], [transpiration])

#mcq(7, [Which sequence correctly describes primary succession?], [Lichens → mosses → grasses → shrubs → trees], [Grasses → lichens → shrubs → trees], [Trees → shrubs → grasses → lichens], [Mosses → lichens → trees])

#mcq(8, [Which of these is the most serious consequence of soil erosion?], [Increased humus], [More soil organisms], [Better water-holding], [Loss of fertile topsoil and reduced crop yield])

#mcq(9, [Green manuring is the practice of], [spraying green dye on crops], [ploughing in a green legume crop], [using only green fertiliser], [planting trees])

#mcq(10, [When sampling a field, the quadrat should be placed], [where the plants are thickest], [only at the edge], [in the shade only], [at random])

#mcq(11, [The base that occurs in RNA but not in DNA is], [uracil], [thymine], [adenine], [cytosine])

#mcq(12, [In the cross TtYy × TtYy, the proportion of offspring showing both recessive phenotypes is], [3/16], [9/16], [1/16], [1/4])

#mcq(13, [Artificial selection differs from natural selection because], [it is slower], [it produces no change], [it acts only on plants], [the selecting agent is human])

#mcq(14, [Evolution occurs in], [an individual organism], [a population over many generations], [a single cell], [one breeding season])

#mcq(15, [An organism that lives in the same habitat as another but eats different food occupies], [the same niche], [no niche], [a different niche], [the same population])

#mcq(16, [Chemicals that kill pests but also kill their predators tend to cause], [a resurgence of the pest later], [a permanent fall in the pest], [no change], [an increase in crop yield])

#mcq(17, [Ammonification is the release of ammonia from], [dead organic matter], [nitrate], [nitrogen gas], [rock minerals])

#mcq(18, [Which of these reduces the greenhouse effect?], [Burning more coal], [Increasing cattle numbers], [Deforestation], [Planting more trees])

#mcq(19, [The products absorbed from the rumen include], [glucose only], [starch], [volatile fatty acids], [cellulose])

#mcq(20, [Temperature in an ecological survey should be measured], [in direct sunlight], [in the shade at the same height each time], [only at noon], [with a ruler])

#mcq(21, [The main source of genetic variation in meiosis is], [replication], [the G2 phase], [crossing over and independent assortment], [cytokinesis])

#mcq(22, [The chance that a family with three children has all boys is], [1/2], [1/8], [1/4], [1/16])

#mcq(23, [A mutation that is lethal acts by], [preventing the organism from surviving to reproduce], [improving survival], [having no effect], [always causing cancer])

#mcq(24, [Fossils of the same species found on two continents separated by an ocean suggest that], [the species evolved twice], [the fossils are fake], [the species could swim], [the continents were once joined])

#mcq(25, [A belt transect differs from a line transect in that it], [uses no tape], [counts only animals], [uses quadrats at intervals along the line], [is not random])

#mcq(26, [Which relationship would be written (+, −)?], [Mutualism], [Commensalism], [Competition], [Parasitism])

#mcq(27, [Soil pH can be raised by adding], [calcium carbonate (lime)], [ammonium sulphate], [sodium chloride], [compost only])

#mcq(28, [Eutrophication is a problem in], [fast-flowing rivers only], [lakes and slow-moving water], [the open ocean], [dry savanna])

#mcq(29, [Smoking preserves fish because smoke], [dries the flesh and deposits antimicrobial compounds], [adds water], [kills only bacteria], [sweetens it])

#mcq(30, [Magnification can also be calculated as], [actual size ÷ image size], [image + actual], [image size ÷ actual size], [image × actual])

#mcq(31, [The spindle fibres attach to the chromosome at the], [telomere], [centromere], [nucleolus], [chromatid arm])

#mcq(32, [A test cross is used to determine], [the sex of an organism], [the number of chromosomes], [the time of flowering], [the genotype of a dominant-looking organism])

#mcq(33, [An adaptation to a hot dry environment is], [a thick layer of blubber], [hibernation], [migration to the north in winter], [aestivation])

#mcq(34, [A population of insects becomes resistant to an insecticide because], [the insects learned to resist], [the insecticide caused a needed mutation], [resistant individuals survived and reproduced], [all the insects mutated at once])

#mcq(35, [Ecological equivalents are species that], [share the same habitat], [share the same niche in different places], [are always closely related], [compete for the same mate])

#mcq(36, [The length of a food chain is limited mainly by], [the loss of energy at each transfer], [the number of species], [the size of the habitat], [the amount of rainfall])

#mcq(37, [A legume grown on nitrogen-poor soil thrives because it], [absorbs nitrate faster], [fixes its own nitrogen with *Rhizobium*], [needs no nitrogen], [grows deeper roots])

#mcq(38, [Noise is a pollutant because it], [changes the chemical composition of air], [increases oxygen], [cools the air], [can damage hearing and disturb wildlife])

#mcq(39, [Fish farming is most developed in Nigeria with], [catfish and tilapia], [salmon and cod], [sharks], [whales])

#mcq(40, [Which graph is appropriate for the rate of photosynthesis against light intensity?], [Bar chart], [Pie chart], [Line graph], [Histogram])

